  "description": "Version\u202f1.0 of the configuration is documented below.  The notes indicate that this is a sample configuration for a simple polyethylene\u2011like molecule, and the files *common.cfg* and *polymer.cfg* are to be included.\n\nThe only molecule defined is **polyethylene**, classified as a linear polymer.  Its comment reads: \u201cSimple\u202fPE chain with three carbon atoms and attached hydrogens.\u201d  The atom list comprises three carbons\u2014C1, C2, and C3\u2014each of type \u201cC\u201d with a partial charge of \u20130.12, and three hydrogens\u2014H1, H2, and H3\u2014each of type \u201cH\u201d with a charge of +0.06.  Bond (length) definitions specify two C\u2011C bonds: one between C1 and C2, and another between C2 and C3, both of type \u201cC\u2011C\u201d.  A single angle is defined as C\u2011C\u2011C among C1, C2, and C3.  One dihedral of type \u201cC\u2011C\u2011C\u2011H\u201d connects the atoms C1, C2, C3, and H1.  Finally, an improper torsion of type \u201cC\u2011C\u2011H\u2011H\u201d involves the atoms C2, C1, H2, and H3."
